<title>USA: U.S. DEBT FUTURES TURN MIXED AFTER CLAIMS DATA.</title>
<headline>U.S. DEBT FUTURES TURN MIXED AFTER CLAIMS DATA.</headline>
<text>
<p>Aug 7 - U.S. debt futures were mixed, with Sept T-bonds briefly turning negative after the latest weekly jobless claims. Claims rose to 300,000 Aug 2 week from a revised 275,000 the previous week. Forecast had been for 307,000. Treasury auctions last leg of refunding today, sells $10 bln 30-yr bonds.</p>
<p>((Chicago Derivatives Desk(312)408-8750))</p>
